\section{Translation rules}{

The returned product labels are \code{nvel_primary} and \code{nvel_secondary} with
priorities 1 and 2. Both use inside-bark diameter limits and board-foot
scaled quantity. The secondary product is marked as the pulp restriction's
allowed product. That label does not change its board-foot measurement unit.

Option 14 selects the Pacific Northwest scaling convention, options 21 and 22 the allocated-
section convention, and the other supported options the short-section convention. \code{scribner = 'factor'} selects factors. Other values, including \code{'regional'}, select the table in this
translator.

The option remains in \code{segmentation_policy}. Minimum and maximum lengths and trim are
copied. A one-unit length increment is assigned, and \code{even_or_odd = 2} selects even lengths.

The primary tree diameter minimum and both small-end limits come from their matching fields.

\code{prod}, \code{ht_type}, \code{live}, \code{ctype}, \code{cull}, \code{forest}, and \code{district} are
copied to \code{meta_nvel_} columns. They retain notes and do not apply live-tree,
cull, or geographic behavior to the merchandising calculation. There is
no separate percentage deduction for the source \code{cull} field here.
}

\section{Returned settings}{

\code{products} is the product table described in \link{product_schema}. Numeric \code{stump_ht} is the
record's stump height. Numeric \code{utilization_height} is \code{stump} plus \code{merchantable_length},
used as an upper height cap.

The translator uses this field as a height cap, despite its source definition as a minimum
primary-product length. \code{model_aux} is a list containing numeric
\code{bark_ratio}, which can be missing. Forward its value only when appropriate for the selected
equation.

Lengths use the supplied height unit and the ratio is unitless.
}

\section{Status and missing values}{

No tree codes are returned. Required merchant defaults must be complete. A source-
version mismatch stops translation.

Missing bark ratio is retained and does not request a model default if explicitly passed
onward as missing. A translated table is not evidence of volume. \code{no_feasible_log} identifies a
valid result with no logs in later calculations.
}

